;; MUST-FAIL FIXTURE — the design record (a later change). Sibling of `deploy-wrong-keyset-name.repl-must-fail`.
;;
;; the design record turned ONE pinned keyset name into TWO. The existing fixture was carried forward for
;; the gov pin; this one exists because a second pin with no falsifying test is exactly the
;; state an internal review a finding found the FIRST pin in — reachable, uncovered, and green under
;; mutation. Adding the enforce without adding this file would have re-created that defect on
;; the same line of the same file, one commit after fixing it.
;;
;; 🔴 THE GOV NAME HERE IS CORRECT ON PURPOSE. The gov enforce runs first; if both names were
;; wrong, this fixture would abort on the gov line and pass while asserting nothing about the
;; ops pin — the "a check that cannot fail" shape. Only the ops name is mistyped, so the
;; expected message can come from nowhere else.
;;
;; 🔴 FALSIFIABILITY, MEASURED — AND THE OBVIOUS TEST FOR IT IS WRONG. Deleting the
;; `spt-ops-name` enforce does NOT make this fixture load successfully: it re-loads a module the
;; prelude already deployed, so it then aborts further down on "Table ... already exists". An
;; EXIT-CODE check therefore reports "still fails" and would clear a dead pin. Measured that way
;; first, and it gave exactly that false all-clear.
;; run-tests.sh does not judge it that way — it requires the fixture to fail AND to carry its
;; expected message, so with the enforce deleted it reports "failed for the WRONG reason".
;; That is the real falsification, and it is the one to re-run:
;; with the enforce -> aborts with "spt-ops-name must be the namespace's spt-ops keyset"
;; without it -> aborts with "Table ... already exists" (gate: WRONG reason)
;; The lesson generalises past this file: a must-fail fixture is only pinned by its MESSAGE.
(load "setup.repl")
(begin-tx "fresh deploy whose spt-ops-name is one character wrong")
(env-data
  { "ns": "n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3"
, "upgrade": false
 ;; CORRECT gov name — this fixture is about the ops pin only.
, "spt-gov-name": "n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.spt-gov"
, "spt-gov": { "keys": ["admin-key"], "pred": "keys-all" }
 ;; The correct name ends ".spt-ops". This one ends ".spt-osp".
, "spt-ops-name": "n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.spt-osp"
, "spt-ops": { "keys": ["admin-key"], "pred": "keys-any" } })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(load "../modules/SPT.pact")
(commit-tx)
